---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Read exact-context Rust APIs, or explicitly prepare their documentation artifacts

Usage: pse api [OPTIONS] <CRATE_QUERY> [PATH]

Arguments:
  <CRATE_QUERY>  Exact locked dependency name, name@version or source-qualified Cargo package ID
  [PATH]         Public crate-relative item path; omission lists candidates

Options:
  -C <checkout>
      --search <SEARCH>            Case-insensitive name/documentation search
      --format <FORMAT>            Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --prepare                    Explicitly compile documentation in an isolated context; ordinary lookup never generates it
      --fields <FIELDS>            Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage
      --target <TARGET>            Explicit target triple; default is the pinned rustc's observed host
      --budget <BUDGET>            Limit payload array records; retain complete evidence as an artifact
      --kind <KIND>                [possible values: function, struct, enum, union, trait, type-alias, constant, static, module, macro, other]
      --input <INPUT>
      --output-type <OUTPUT_TYPE>
      --trait-name <TRAIT_NAME>
      --unsafe-only
      --async-only
      --const-only
      --docs                       Expand authored documentation for returned candidates
      --examples                   Expand authored Rust examples and hidden setup; never execute them
      --cursor <CURSOR>            Continue the same immutable artifact/query page; stale contexts refuse
  -h, --help                       Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Read exact-context Rust APIs, or explicitly prepare their documentation artifacts

Usage: pse api [OPTIONS] <CRATE_QUERY> [PATH]

Arguments:
  <CRATE_QUERY>
          Exact locked dependency name, name@version or source-qualified Cargo package ID

  [PATH]
          Public crate-relative item path; omission lists candidates

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --search <SEARCH>
          Case-insensitive name/documentation search

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --prepare
          Explicitly compile documentation in an isolated context; ordinary lookup never generates it

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage

      --target <TARGET>
          Explicit target triple; default is the pinned rustc's observed host

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit payload array records; retain complete evidence as an artifact

      --kind <KIND>
          Possible values:
          - function:   A free or associated function
          - struct:     A struct declaration
          - enum:       An enum declaration
          - union:      A union declaration
          - trait:      A trait or trait alias
          - type-alias: A type alias
          - constant:   A constant or associated constant
          - static:     A static declaration
          - module:     A module declaration
          - macro:      A declarative or procedural macro
          - other:      Another rustdoc declaration, retained without guessing its kind

      --input <INPUT>


      --output-type <OUTPUT_TYPE>


      --trait-name <TRAIT_NAME>


      --unsafe-only


      --async-only


      --const-only


      --docs
          Expand authored documentation for returned candidates

      --examples
          Expand authored Rust examples and hidden setup; never execute them

      --cursor <CURSOR>
          Continue the same immutable artifact/query page; stale contexts refuse

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
